## 1. Usage Grant

Licensor hereby grants you the right to copy, modify, create derivative
works, redistribute, and make non-production use of the Software, subject
to the following conditions:

1.1. You may make production use of the Software, provided such use is not
     a Competing Use, as defined below.

1.2. Any Competing Use requires a separate commercial agreement with
     Licensor. Contact: [TODO: sales/licensing contact email or URL].

"Competing Use" means using the Software's functionality, unmodified or
modified, to (a) offer a product or service to third parties that competes
with any product or service offered by Licensor that itself uses the
Software, or (b) circumvent a paid feature, seat limit, or usage limit of
a product or service offered by Licensor.

## 2. Additional Use Grant (small-deployment carve-out)

Notwithstanding Section 1.2, Production Use that would otherwise be a
Competing Use is nonetheless permitted, without a separate commercial
agreement, for any Organization whose deployment of the Software serves
[TODO: confirm threshold - draft default: 5] or fewer individual Users in
total, counted across every environment that Organization operates.

This carve-out exists so a single company or team can self-host and run
this software for itself, for free, indefinitely, regardless of how the
"Competing Use" restriction above would otherwise apply to a larger
deployment.

